                        "content": "A client with glaucoma is given a prescription for a pilocarpine ocular system. The nurse plans to provide which instruction to the client on how to use the medication?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nThe pilocarpine ocular system has a bilayered membrane surrounding a reservoir of pilocarpine solution. The tiny unit, which is placed in the conjunctival sac, slowly releases medication. The unit needs to be changed once a week. Because the unit may fall out during sleep, the client would check the eye each morning for its presence.",
                        "id": "0a8a66442a154e78812e43542b015cec",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
